Package: uknpm
Title: UK Nutrient Profile Model and Healthiness Assessment Approaches
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Geoffrey", "Manda", email = "author@example.com", role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Nutrition Research", role = "cph")
  )
Description: Comprehensive implementation of UK food and beverage healthiness
    assessment models and statutory regulatory frameworks. Includes the UK
    Nutrient Profile Model (NPM 2004/2005 Technical Guidance 2011 and NPM 2018
    consultation draft) for classifying foods and drinks as High in Fat, Salt,
    or Sugar (HFSS) under advertising, placement, and promotional restrictions.
    Also provides front-of-pack Multiple Traffic Light (MTL) labelling (DHSC
    2013/2016), UK calorie, salt, and sugar reduction programme targets (PHE /
    OHID 2024), Soft Drinks Industry Levy (SDIL) thresholds, and integrated
    multi-metric healthiness evaluation for out-of-home and retail nutrition
    datasets.
